st-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#17-give-your-everyday-bag-one-hook-by-the-door">17. Give your everyday bag one hook by the door</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#18-empty-your-bag-once-a-week">18. Empty your bag once a week</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#common-purse-storage-mistakes">Common Purse Storage Mistakes</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#purse-and-handbag-storage-faq">Purse and Handbag Storage FAQ</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-you-store-purses-so-they-keep-their-shape">How do you store purses so they keep their shape?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-you-store-a-lot-of-purses-in-a-small-space">How do you store a lot of purses in a small space?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#what-are-the-best-handbag-storage-ideas-for-a-closet">What are the best handbag storage ideas for a closet?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#is-it-bad-to-hang-purses">Is it bad to hang purses?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#should-handbags-be-stored-in-plastic">Should handbags be stored in plastic?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#where-should-i-store-handbags-in-a-bedroom">Where should I store handbags in a bedroom?</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#final-thoughts">Final Thoughts</a></li></ul></div></nav>


<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Store Each Bag by Its Shape</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Most purse storage problems come from treating every bag the same. A structured handbag keeps its shape only if it stands on its base and nothing presses on it. A soft tote is happy on a hook. Crossbody bags need their straps controlled, and clutches and wallets disappear unless they have a drawer. Sort your bags into these four groups first, and the right storage becomes obvious.</p>



<figure class="dsh-diagram" style="margin:2em 0;"><svg viewBox="0 0 1200 900" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="dspu-t dspu-d" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="font-family:Poppins,'Helvetica Neue',Arial,sans-serif;height:auto;display:block;border-radius:12px;"><title id="dspu-t">How to store four kinds of bags</title><desc id="dspu-d">Four kinds of bags and how to store each. Structured handbags: best upright on a shelf with dividers, stuffed to hold their shape; avoid stacking bags in a pile. Totes and soft bags: best on a wide hook or in an open bin, folded loosely; avoid heavy bags on thin hooks. Crossbody bags: best on hooks or in a hanging organizer with the strap tucked inside; avoid tangled straps in a pile. Clutches and wallets: best filed upright in a drawer with dividers; avoid leaving them loose on an open shelf. Tip: keep leather dry, dark and filled, with acid-free tissue, cotton dust bags and 45 to 55 percent humidity, based on the Canadian Conservation Institute.</desc><rect width="1200" height="900" fill="#F7F1E9"/><text x="60" y="84" font-size="44" font-weight="700" fill="#342E2A">Store Each Bag by Its Shape</text><text x="60" y="124" font-size="24" fill="#6E645C">four kinds of bags, four kinds of storage</text><text x="1140" y="84" font-size="20" fill="#C85A32" text-anchor="end">dailyspacehacks.com</text><rect x="60" y="160" width="520" height="266" rx="16" fill="#FFFFFF" stroke="#D8CBBB" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="60" y="160" width="520" height="8" rx="4" fill="#8FA689"/><circle cx="180" cy="302" r="100" fill="#DCE5D6" opacity="0.6"/><path d="M146 286 Q180 230 214 286" fill="none" stroke="#342E2A" stroke-width="7" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M118 360 L132 286 L228 286 L242 360 Z" fill="#8FA689" stroke="#342E2A" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M132 286 L180 314 L228 286" fill="none" stroke="#342E2A" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="180" cy="314" r="5" fill="#D9B48A" stroke="#342E2A" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="300" y="218" font-size="